details.image_prompt:
[
  {
    "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. Composition is a 3/4 overhead shot at a 40-degree angle, showing two white matte ceramic plates placed on an aged oak wood surface. The primary plate in the foreground is centered, with the second plate slightly blurred in the background. Each plate features a heap of very thin, delicate golden-brown whole-wheat angel hair pasta tossed with tender, bright green 2-inch asparagus segments and pieces of pan-seared turkey breast cutlets with golden-brown, caramelized edges. The components are intermingled but distinct, showing texture variation between the firm turkey and soft pasta. A glossy, light lemon-caper reduction clings to the pasta strands, with visible small, dark caper buds and flecks of minced garlic scattered throughout. A fresh dusting of roughly chopped flat-leaf parsley garnishes the top. Soft natural side light from a window on the left creates subtle highlights on the sauce-coated pasta and soft, realistic shadows. Props include a single wooden fork resting casually next to the foreground plate and a small pile of whole capers and a halved lemon sitting on the wood surface. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating — lived-in, warm, authentic. Slight natural imperfections: an asymmetric garnish placement, a small sauce drip on the plate rim, slightly uneven browning on the turkey. Include subtle traces of the cooking process: a stray parsley leaf on the table, a slight oil sheen on the wood. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. Warm, golden-hour color temperature. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces."
  }
]
